This input set does not support another synthesis; it supports three repairs, one placement fix, and a reason to stop synthesising. The three commitment-surfaces now in view converge — same retained pieces (expiry-and-review, explicit imbalance surfacing), same open case (collapsed engagement), same salvage list — and p.carry.0 already fused their sources into a probe sequence. I also note what is not in front of me: I see the account and the objection only by their commitments, and the negotiation-economy rival only as quoted inside p.carry.0. That absence says what I can currently see, nothing about what happened earlier; but it means the rival's grounds are now carried at one remove, a dependence flagged below rather than smoothed over. For the asker, the practical opening is unchanged: the first move is still visible, self-binding ownership of one domain. What follows revises what comes after.

Retained, with grounds attached rather than re-derived: the five-step order (self-binding partition; money conversion; week-sized deals for the remnant; exits before meetings; review moved from engine to check), because its ordering principle — least buy-in first — rests on the objection's non-attendance point as carried by p.carry.0 and on the rival's ordering principle, and because each step already arrives carrying a discriminating observation, the design rule the objection's 'not a test, a bet' challenge was converted into. Also retained: co-authored records scaled to stakes (the contested-record argument); one lever at a time with pauses (bundling destroys the signal); the friendship-maintenance condition with conflict-migration as its early warning. One ground the sequence was using without naming: the original task's changing work schedules. Schedule volatility is the material's own reason to prefer seven-day, in-the-moment allocation over any standing rota, and I attach it explicitly to the week-sized deal so a later revision cannot quietly drop it and leave that step under-argued.

Placement fix. p.carry.0 calls for consulting the third flatmate 'before any avoider-directed move' but never slots the consultation into the sequence. It sits in parallel, not in line: it gates step four (the exits) and the fallback one-to-one, and it does not gate steps one to three, which are either unilateral (partition) or topic-narrow (money, week deals) and so do not turn on how the avoider is portrayed. The inherited constraint stands unchanged: error-correction only, dropped if it cannot be structured so as to be unexperienceable as recruitment.

First repair — the exit diagnostic needs a validity condition. p.carry.0 scores an exit taken with relief as evidence that governance was the object, and inherits the objection's warning that refusal is multiply interpretable. Neither text states the precondition under which refusal is interpretable at all. Refusal of an exit that is worse than engagement on any plausible reading of the avoider's position is evidence about the offer, not about governance, grievance, or friendship. So before the observation is scored, the exit must pass a generosity test: at least as good as continued engagement under the most sympathetic available reading of what the avoider wants (for instance, a permanent defined domain with no meeting attendance, or a larger money share in lieu of rota participation), offered without penalty and without a story attached. This is my addition, not a claim any input made; its ground is the principle the sequence already relies on, that choice behaviour is evidence only when the chooser faced a live alternative.

Second repair — the unowned commons, partially discharged. p.carry.0 left this open: if exits and money both fail, something remains that someone absorbs, prices, or lets slide, and letting it slide rebuilds the tacit expectations that generate disputes, by the account's own mechanism. A step short of solution is available from existing pieces: declare the neglect. Name the commons as a named unowned domain, state the (possibly low) standard it will be kept to, state who if anyone absorbs overflow, date it, and expose it to the same review as the fairness fork. The account's mechanism generates disputes from unspoken expectations, not from low standards as such; a declared low standard is an expectation nobody can later reinterpret — precisely the property the co-authored-record revision was built to secure. This allocates no labour; it removes the dispute-generator from the unallocated remainder. It also answers, partially, the admitted weakness in dropping 'silence is not agreement': declared neglect makes the status quo explicit without conscripting anyone. If even this declaration cannot be obtained, that failure is data and feeds the threshold below rather than reverting to quiet absorption. Sequencing note: the declaration occurs late and conditionally, so one-lever discipline is untouched.

Third repair — the boundary case gets a threshold, not a script. p.carry.0 declined to script the conversation for when a chore problem becomes a question about the arrangement, and that decline stands. But 'leave it open' should not decay into 'never notice.' Proposed stop-conditions for the chore sequence, any two sufficient: a generous exit (per the test above) refused together with any engagement across more than one cycle; on the migration probe, dispute content predominantly about persons rather than tasks; flatmate three, if consultable, independently reporting the same pattern. Tripping the threshold does not say what to do next; it says the sequence is being applied to the wrong problem, and that continuing it past that point would itself be the litigant failure mode the whole construction is sworn to avoid. The thresholds are my conjecture — uncalibrated, criticizable, revisable — offered so the open problem acquires an observable edge.

Finally, the carrying itself gets a stopping rule. Every step of the sequence is evidence-hungry by construction, and no observation can arrive through this template; the commitments now in view add convergence, not evidence. A further synthesis without an outcome report from the flat would rearrange rather than improve. So the proposal is: the sequence stands as converged; the most useful next input is a report from any attempted step; failing that, the next carry should retain rather than extend — and should re-verify the rival's claim, including its self-named local disconfirmation (a clear written arrangement actually ending the disputes), against the rival's own text if that text is available, since I hold it only through p.carry.0's mediation.